            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0637" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1631/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-03T17:00:00-06:00">May 3, 1935—5 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. With reference to the Department’s telegram 26, May 1, noon, schedule I and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> were handed to the Salvadoran
                    Government today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
